# The city route of the hand-off trace (cpu/handoff-trace work): boot -> title -> city, a standing segment (roam) and a
# wall-time drive (drive), both uncapped, then a 60 FPS cap. Run it with real-time steps (no --mcla_fixed_dt) and --mcla_fps=0
# (uncapped) and, for the trace, --handoff_trace=true --handoff_trace_run=false --handoff_trace_file=<run folder>\handoff.hotrace:
# the trace then records only the windows below (`set handoff_trace_run true` ... `false`, 6 s each), and the file is written at
# the end (`set handoff_trace_dump true`). Without --handoff_trace the same script runs with nothing recorded (every `set` of
# the handoff_trace_* options is then ignored), so that the frame times of the windows can be compared with and without the
# trace: the `mark`s w_* ... w_*_end bracket each window in frames.csv.
# Marks: title, map_zoom, free_roam, roam, w_roam, w_roam_end, drive, w_drive, w_drive_end, settle, cap60, w_cap60, w_cap60_end, end.
wait 8s
mark title
press_until start left_title every=2s timeout=90s
mark map_zoom
wait_until roam 180s
mark free_roam
wait 8s
mark roam
wait 2s
set handoff_trace_label roam
mark w_roam
set handoff_trace_run true
wait 6s
set handoff_trace_run false
mark w_roam_end
wait 2s
trigger rt 1 0.35s
trigger rt 0.6
stick lx 1 0.28s
trigger rt 1
mark drive
wait 3s
set handoff_trace_label drive
mark w_drive
set handoff_trace_run true
wait 6s
set handoff_trace_run false
mark w_drive_end
wait 3s
release all
set mcla_fps 60
mark settle
wait 4s
mark cap60
set handoff_trace_label cap60
mark w_cap60
set handoff_trace_run true
wait 6s
set handoff_trace_run false
mark w_cap60_end
wait 1s
set mcla_fps 0
mark end
set handoff_trace_dump true
wait 4s
